* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-real-divider (issue #159, Part of #16)
* NOMINAL-CORNER, PRE-LAYOUT closed-loop deck, two arms from ONE template.
*
*   ARM=control : feedback = unchanged behavioural XSPICE divide-by-64
*                 (same d_dff toggle chain as RECORD-003/005's decks).
*   ARM=real    : feedback = committed transistor-level `divider_chain`
*                 (repaired, #112/#121), P5..P0 = 000000 (N = 64).
*
* Everything outside the arm block marker is byte-identical between arms
* (run.sh renders both from this file): rails, reference, supplies, bias
* currents, loop filter, VCO word, .ic on vctrl / ring1, solver options,
* TSTOP/TPRINT/TMAX. The real arm additionally needs latch .ic statements on
* the divider's 13 flops (the block has no reset; see RECORD-001) -- those
* are the only arm-specific initial conditions and are declared in the arm
* block. `vdd_div` exists in BOTH arms (unloaded in the control arm).
*
* Substitutions vs the production composition (all disclosed in RECORD-001):
*   S1 loop_filter XC1/XC2 (cap_cmomi) -> ideal caps at campaign values.
*   S2 vco XCDECAP stripped (same precedent as the campaign decks).
*   S3 cp IBP/ICP/IBN/ICN driven by ideal @IREF@ current sources.
*   S4 b0/b1 held at rails by ideal sources; REF is an ideal pulse source.
*   S5 lock_detector NOT instantiated.
*   S6 control arm only: ideal behavioural divider.
*   S7 real arm only: latch .ic symmetry break on divider flops.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include pll_blocks_realdiv.spice

Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

Vdd_pfd vdd_pfd 0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_cp  vdd_cp  0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_vco vdd_vco 0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_div vdd_div 0 dc @VDD@

Vref ref 0 pulse(0 @VDD@ 0 100p 100p @TREFH@ @TREF@)
Vb0 b0 0 dc @B0V@
Vb1 b1 0 dc @B1V@

Irefbp ibp 0 dc @IREF@
Irefcp icp 0 dc @IREF@
Irefbn 0 ibn dc @IREF@
Irefcn 0 icn dc @IREF@

XPFD ref fb up dn vdd_pfd 0 pfd
XCP up dn ibp icp ibn icn vctrl vdd_cp 0 cp
XLF vctrl 0 loop_filter
XVCO vctrl b0 b1 clk vdd_vco 0 vco

* ---- arm block begin ----
@ARM_BLOCK@
* ---- arm block end ----

.ic v(vctrl)=@VC0@
.ic v(xvco.ring1)=0.5

* Save only what the measurements and extraction need: with default save-all the
* real arm exhausts ngspice memory (see RECORD-001, attempt 1). Identical in both arms.
.save v(ref) v(fb) v(vctrl) v(clk) i(Vdd_pfd) i(Vdd_cp) i(Vdd_vco) i(Vdd_div)
.tran @TPRINT@ @TSTOP@ 0 @TMAX@

.control
run
meas tran i_pfd avg i(Vdd_pfd) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_cp  avg i(Vdd_cp)  from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_vco avg i(Vdd_vco) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_div avg i(Vdd_div) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_avg avg v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_max max v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_min min v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
print i_pfd i_cp i_vco i_div vc_avg vc_max vc_min
linearize v(ref) v(fb) v(vctrl) v(clk)
wrdata wave.dat v(ref) v(fb) v(vctrl) v(clk)
.endc
.end
